WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Welcome to the Vancomyzer tutorial.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:03.820
Let's get started.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.720
Think of a GPS estimating arrival time across a small city.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.060
Usual travel patterns provide a starting estimate;

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.420
details of your trip personalize it.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.360
Bayesian dosing starts with a population model, then uses patient characteristics

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.800
to personalize the estimate.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.840
Measured concentrations, with reliable dose and sample times, update it like new

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.780
traffic information.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.940
Uncertainty remains: poor inputs or a poorly matched model can mislead.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.420
The estimate still needs clinical review.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.540
Explore Vancomyzer with this fictional adult example and begin by checking recent vancomycin

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.120
doses at every facility.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.820
Review medication administration and transfer records to confirm the amount given and

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.980
exact infusion and blood draw times, because a transferred patient may already have received

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.140
a loading dose and should not automatically receive another.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:04.250
In empiric, enter age, sex, weight, height and serum creatinine, then confirm renal replacement

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.650
status and review frailty when relevant.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.410
This tool supports adults receiving intermittent intravenous vancomycin rather than dialysis

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.450
dosing, so calculate and inspect the regimen and predicted exposure while remembering

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.590
that results before measured levels remain population estimates and the graph and candidate

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.650
regimens show predictions to review.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.760
Review the dose, actual infusion duration and number of doses given, then enter the measured

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.980
concentration with exact blood draw and infusion times.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.520
Without a measured level, any available prediction remains based on the prior model.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.920
Never enter a predicted concentration as a measured result.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.800
Changed, held or missed maintenance doses

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.800
are not supported by this workflow.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:56.680
Review the curve, candidate regimens and model limitations using the guideline AUC target

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:02.060
of 400 to 600 for serious invasive MRSA infection when the MIC is one.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:07.800
Follow institutional monitoring protocols with two levels preferred for Bayesian estimation,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.960
reassess when kidney function changes and document your plan remembering that Vancomyzer

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.300
still awaits independent patient validation.